schema: "0.4"
id: sem-details-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-details
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-details>` element — the CONTAINER
    that groups one or more `<sem-detail>` prose passages whose `<highlight>`
    words are recall targets. One example page per display mode the container
    provides, rendered in the minimal-tech theme on a dark slate canvas
    (bg #0f172a, surface #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0, accent #60a5fa). TWO stacked
    example pages, each a container holding TWO prose passages inside a
    browser-chrome frame, labeled with a small mono uppercase caption.

    Page 1 — caption "PLAIN (default)". The container holds two short prose
    passages, each in a hairline #334155 rounded card (12px radius). Passage 1:
    "The OIDC token travels in the Authorization header." with "Authorization"
    emphasized — an accent-blue tint behind the text at 18% opacity (a soft
    luminous wash, color(srgb 0.376 0.647 0.980 / 0.18)), 4px rounded corners,
    a few pixels of horizontal padding, the glyphs fully saturated foreground
    color and completely legible. Passage 2: "A refresh grant mints a new
    access token without a new login." with "access token" emphasized the same
    way. Nothing is occluded; the container reads as one grouped recall passage.
    This is the default — `view-as` omitted IS plain.

    Page 2 — caption "QUIZ". The identical container and the identical two
    passages with the same words, but each emphasized word is occluded: a solid
    slate chip (#475569), rounded 4px, at least 3ch wide, no visible glyphs —
    a self-check recall mask with a subtle pointer affordance. One chip is
    shown revealed beside a still-occluded chip: the revealed word is the
    accent-tinted, fully legible word from page 1, demonstrating the one-way
    per-item reveal (click or Enter/Space). The prose wording is identical to
    page 1 — only the interaction model changes; `view-as` is display-only
    sugar and never rewrites the words.

    Typography: clean system sans (Inter-like), 16px body, 1.6 line height,
    generous margins. No extra chrome, no buttons other than the caption
    labels, no pointer cursors drawn as graphics.
  negative: >
    occluded or blurred text on the plain page; black bars over text;
    strikethrough; redaction-marker aesthetic on page 1; the container drawn
    as a button, tab strip, accordion or disclosure widget; fewer than two
    passages per container; different words between the plain and quiz pages;
    neon glow; drop shadows on text; italic highlight text; more than two
    example pages; light background; watermark; lorem ipsum in the caption
    labels.
  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline #334155 borders, generous
    negative space. Looks like a panel from a design-system guide.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-details/sem-details-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-details/sem-details-quiz-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-details/sem-details-quiz-render-reveal-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-details-ux-design.png

requirements:
  modes:
    - id: plain
      label: "PLAIN (default)"
      must_show:
        - the container holding two prose passages, each in a hairline card
        - every word readable, highlights as an accent-blue tint behind the
          text at reduced opacity (18%), 4px rounded corners, horizontal padding
        - highlighted glyphs in the normal foreground color, full contrast
      must_never:
        - occlude, blur, bar or mask any highlighted text
        - render a highlight as an opaque filled block that hides glyphs
        - style the container as clickable chrome (button, tab, accordion)
    - id: quiz
      label: "QUIZ"
      must_show:
        - the same two passages and the same words, highlights replaced by
          solid slate occlusion chips (#475569), rounded, min 3ch wide, no glyphs
        - one chip revealed beside a still-occluded chip: the accent-tinted,
          fully legible word from the plain page
        - keyboard/click reveal affordance implied, one-way per item
      must_never:
        - leave quiz-view occlusion on the plain page
        - reveal more than the demonstrated item at once
        - change the passage wording away from the plain page

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    plain-legibility:
      weight: 0.4
      description: >
        Page 1's highlighted words are fully readable — normal foreground
        glyphs over a light accent tint; the tint reads as emphasis, and the
        container's two passages read as one grouped prose block.
      fail_signals:
        - highlighted text hidden behind an opaque block
        - highlighted text blurred, crossed out, or lower-contrast
        - occlusion chip present on the plain page
    quiz-occlusion:
      weight: 0.3
      description: >
        Page 2 occludes each recall target as a solid rounded chip with no
        visible glyphs, and shows one accent-tinted revealed state beside it.
      fail_signals:
        - quiz chip shows ghosted or partially readable glyphs
        - revealed state missing or occluded
        - quiz wording differs from the plain page
    container-grouping:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        Both pages show a container of two passages — the container reads as a
        group of passages, never as a single passage or as clickable chrome.
      fail_signals:
        - only one passage per container
        - container drawn as a button, tab strip, or accordion
    theme-fidelity:
      weight: 0.1
      description: >
        Dark minimal-tech palette (#0f172a bg, #60a5fa accent), hairline
        borders, mono uppercase captions, two labeled example pages.
      fail_signals:
        - light background or multiple accent hues
        - more or fewer than two labeled pages
        - watermark, lorem ipsum, decorative noise
  reject_if:
    - the plain page occludes or hides any text
    - the two pages show different prose wording
    - any page shows illegible body copy